======================
Simple Password Store
by Jason Donenfeld
   Jason@zx2c4.com
======================

This Linux-only bp fork encrypts passwords using gpg and
places the encrypted password in a directory. It can generate new passwords
and keep track of old ones.

Visit the project page for more information: http://www.passwordstore.org/

Please see the man page for documentation and examples.

Depends on:
- bash
  http://www.gnu.org/software/bash/
- GnuPG2
  http://www.gnupg.org/
- git (optional)
  http://www.git-scm.com/
- xclip (optional, for X11 environments)
  http://sourceforge.net/projects/xclip/
- wl-clipboard (optional, installed separately for Wayland environments)
  https://github.com/bugaevc/wl-clipboard
- bx, diffutils, findutils, sed, and procps
  (directory listings are built in; tree is not required)
- GNU getopt
  http://www.kernel.org/pub/linux/utils/util-linux/
  http://software.frodo.looijaard.name/getopt/
- qrencode (optional)
  https://fukuchi.org/works/qrencode/

See ../README.md for bp packaging and test instructions.
